#
# Lychee link-checker exclusions. Each entry below is a URL pattern
# that's intentionally referenced in the docs but doesn't resolve to
# a browseable page — they're load-bearing endpoints (OIDC issuers,
# API URLs) or example placeholders. Format: one regex per line,
# matched against the full URL.

# GitHub Actions OIDC issuer. This is the canonical `iss` value the
# Fulcio cert must claim for `--method=sigstore` verification; the
# URL is referenced in --cert-oidc-issuer flag documentation. It's
# an OIDC endpoint, not a browseable page — anonymous GET returns 404.
^https://token\.actions\.githubusercontent\.com/?$

# REUSE API status / info endpoints. The README badge pulls JSON
# from the status endpoint (which works); the click-through goes to
# /info/... which returns 404 until the project is indexed at
# api.reuse.software.
^https://api\.reuse\.software/(info|status)/.*$

# Google Cloud Console URLs in publishing.md. These are canonical
# pointers ("enable this API", "create a service account") that
# adopters need to follow while signed in. Anonymous requests return
# a 302 to the Google login page; lychee reports the 302 as broken.
^https://console\.cloud\.google\.com/.*$

# Integration testsuite repo. Lives at
# github.com/diggsweden/reusable-ci-blackbox-tests but isn't currently
# a public repo (planned). Until publication, lychee 404s on it; once
# published this line can come out.
^https://github\.com/diggsweden/reusable-ci-blackbox-tests/?$

# NTIA "SBOM Minimum Elements" report PDF. The canonical citation for
# the CISA 3-layer SBOM baseline; ntia.gov serves an incomplete TLS
# chain that lychee's trust store rejects. The URL itself is correct.
^https://www\.ntia\.gov/sites/default/files/publications/sbom_minimum_elements_report_0\.pdf$
